BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-04@btw2026
DTSTART:20260604T183000
DTEND:20260604T200000
SUMMARY:First Touch & Receiving
LOCATION:Park School
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nReceiving to feet and turning to face goal\nDirectiona
 l first touch to set up a pass or dribble\nReceiving on the back foot and p
 laying away from pressure\nSettling a driven pass with a soft inside-of-foo
 t touch\nChecking off a defender to create space before receiving\nBody sha
 pe and foot orientation before the ball arrives
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-05@btw2026
DTSTART:20260605T151500
DTEND:20260605T164500
SUMMARY:Passing & Combination Play
LOCATION:Cypress Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nWall pass: give and go to break the defensive line\nTh
 ird-man run: timing a late run to receive after a combination\nWeight and a
 ccuracy of short passes under pressure\nOne-touch passing to maintain speed
  of play\nPlaying through a press as a unit of three\nSwitching the point o
 f attack with a driven pass
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-07@btw2026
DTSTART:20260607T163000
DTEND:20260607T180000
SUMMARY:1v1 Attacking vs. Defending
LOCATION:Cypress Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nStep-over\, scissors\, or Cruyff turn to beat a defend
 er\nCommitting the defender before attempting a move\nJockeying: staying go
 al-side and on feet under pressure\nForcing the attacker onto their weak fo
 ot\nWinning the ball back with a clean tackle when the moment is right\nDri
 bbling with purpose\, head up\, exploit space after the move
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-08@btw2026
DTSTART:20260608T153000
DTEND:20260608T170000
SUMMARY:1v1 Attacking vs. Defending
LOCATION:Cypress Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nStep-over\, scissors\, or Cruyff turn to beat a defend
 er\nCommitting the defender before attempting a move\nJockeying: staying go
 al-side and on feet under pressure\nForcing the attacker onto their weak fo
 ot\nWinning the ball back with a clean tackle when the moment is right\nDri
 bbling with purpose\, head up\, exploit space after the move
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-09@btw2026
DTSTART:20260609T183000
DTEND:20260609T200000
SUMMARY:First Touch & Receiving
LOCATION:Park School
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nChest control and immediate lay-off or turn\nThigh con
 trol from a lofted ball and playing under pressure\nHalf-volley control on 
 a bouncing ball\nHeading down to a teammate or into space\nCatching a dropp
 ing ball on the instep and moving forward\nWinning the second ball after an
  aerial contest
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-12@btw2026
DTSTART:20260612T153000
DTEND:20260612T170000
SUMMARY:First Touch + Finishing vs. Defensive Pressure
LOCATION:Cypress Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nFirst touch / ball control\nPlaced finish into the far
  corner under pressure\nOne-touch finish from a cut-back or low cross\nClos
 ing down a shooter to force a rushed attempt\nShot power vs. placement: cho
 osing the right technique\nFinishing with the weaker foot from a realistic 
 position\nBlock tackle or interception to prevent a shot on goal
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-15@btw2026
DTSTART:20260615T180000
DTEND:20260615T193000
SUMMARY:Ball Control & First Touch
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nJuggling with the instep and inside of the foot\nCatch
 ing a dropping ball on the instep and moving forward
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-16@btw2026
DTSTART:20260616T180000
DTEND:20260616T193000
SUMMARY:First Touch & Passing
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nOne and two-touch play in tight spaces under pressure
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-18@btw2026
DTSTART:20260618T170000
DTEND:20260618T183000
SUMMARY:Aerial Duels & Crossing
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nTracking the ball in the air\nJudging when to challeng
 e in the air vs read a bounce\nEarly cross delivery before the fullback can
  close\nNear-post run\nFar-post run\nDefending a cross: Tracking a far-post
  runner as a centerback
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-22@btw2026
DTSTART:20260622T180000
DTEND:20260622T193000
SUMMARY:First Touch & Receiving
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nShielding the ball on the first touch to protect posse
 ssion\nFake receive: letting the ball run to lose a tight marker\nScanning 
 before the ball arrives to choose touch direction\nOne-touch layoff when re
 ceiving under a high press\nBreaking the press line with a single forward t
 ouch\nStaying calm and composed when receiving in tight space
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-23@btw2026
DTSTART:20260623T180000
DTEND:20260623T193000
SUMMARY:Passing & Combination Play
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nRondo: maintaining possession under a high press\nIden
 tifying and passing to the free player\nWeight of pass when playing into a 
 striker's feet\nQuick combination in the final third to create a shooting o
 pportunity\nPlaying the killer pass through or over the defensive line\nPat
 ience in possession: when to recycle vs. when to play forward
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-25@btw2026
DTSTART:20260625T180000
DTEND:20260625T193000
SUMMARY:Finishing vs. Defensive Pressure
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nGK 1v1: reading the goalkeeper's position\nChip finish
  when GK is off the line\nDriven low finish across the body past a GK\nReco
 very run to deny a through ball before the finish\nComposure in front of go
 al: slowing the moment down\nDecision-making: shoot vs. square vs. hold up
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-26@btw2026
DTSTART:20260626T080000
DTEND:20260626T100000
SUMMARY:1v1 Attacking vs. Defending
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nHolding up play with back to goal under physical press
 ure\nShielding the ball and drawing a foul\nFlicking on or laying off from 
 a back-to-goal position\nSpinning off a marker into space behind the defens
 e\nFronting a striker: physical positioning to prevent the turn\nTiming a t
 ackle when a forward tries to spin
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-29@btw2026
DTSTART:20260629T180000
DTEND:20260629T193000
SUMMARY:Passing & Combination Play
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nRondo: maintaining possession under a high press\nIden
 tifying and passing to the free player\nWeight of pass when playing into a 
 striker's feet\nQuick combination in the final third to create a shooting o
 pportunity\nPlaying the killer pass through or over the defensive line\nPat
 ience in possession: when to recycle vs. when to play forward
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-06-30@btw2026
DTSTART:20260630T180000
DTEND:20260630T193000
SUMMARY:Crossing & Aerial Duels
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nGetting to the byline and delivering a low cut-back\nL
 ate run from midfield to meet the cut-back and shoot\nHolding a defensive l
 ine as runners attack the cut-back\nFirst-time finish from a low cut-back a
 cross the box\nDisguising cross direction to delay the defensive shift\nCov
 ering the cut-back channel as a defending fullback
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-07-02@btw2026
DTSTART:20260702T180000
DTEND:20260702T193000
SUMMARY:First Touch & Receiving
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nShoulder check before receiving to identify pressure\n
 Half-turn technique: opening the body to receive facing forward\nUsing peri
 pheral vision to choose touch direction before contact\nReceiving between l
 ines and instantly playing forward\nFirst touch away from pressure in a con
 gested midfield\nControlling the tempo of the game through a composed first
  touch
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-07-03@btw2026
DTSTART:20260703T080000
DTEND:20260703T100000
SUMMARY:Crossing & Aerial Duels
LOCATION:Harry Downes Field
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nAttacking a corner kick delivery: near post and far po
 st runs\nZonal marking on set pieces: attacking the ball at highest point\n
 Man-marking assignment on corners: staying with the runner\nHeading techniq
 ue for both attacking and defensive headers\nSecond ball reaction after a c
 leared set piece\nGoalkeeper distribution from a set piece clearance
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:tech-2026-07-05@btw2026
DTSTART:20260705T163000
DTEND:20260705T180000
SUMMARY:1v1 Attacking vs. Defending
LOCATION:Park School
DESCRIPTION:Skills:\nPressing trigger: when and how to press the ball\nEsca
 pe from a press: one-touch away from pressure\nBall protection on the dribb
 le in a high-pressure situation\nCoordinated pressing as a pair to cut off 
 passing lanes\nWinning the ball back high up the pitch from the front\nCoun
 tering immediately after winning possession in the press
END:VEVENT
